  "body": "Since matrix.org's synapse was restarted on Oct 11, it seems like ReplicationSendEventRestServlet is using roughly twice as much CPU per request. This makes for quite a noticeable change in CPU usage (even though it's only a few % of a core).\r\n\r\n<img width=\"916\" alt=\"Screenshot 2019-10-29 at 22 28 43\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1294269/67814333-b67c8700-fa9b-11e9-9fc2-8dd290b3edb2.png\">\r\n<img width=\"1841\" alt=\"Screenshot 2019-10-29 at 22 31 13\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1294269/67814381-d90ea000-fa9b-11e9-8a4a-728b87465c93.png\">\r\n\r\nI found this while wondering why the synapse master started taking 20-30% more CPU as of Oct 14th.",
